    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0241" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/15352: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-07T19:00:00+01:00">September 7,
                            1939—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 7—2:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1502. Your 813, September 6, 6 p.m.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d209-f1"/> The
                    Department’s inquiry was discussed informally at the Foreign Office today. They
                    hope in <pb facs="0242" n="238" xml:id="pg238"/> the immediate future to be in a
                    position to exchange views with us. It was stated informally, however, that in
                    the last analysis the position that Great Britain would have to take will, in
                    view of existing circumstances, have to depend on what the position of the
                    United States is to be.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d209-f1" n="8" xml:id="d209-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see first paragraph of telegram No. 276, September 6, 6 p.m., to the
                    Chargé in Japan, <ref target="frus1931-41v02#pg_12">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 12</ref>.</p>
            </note>
